WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.174
Use goal, owners, values, evidence, rules and notice.

00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:07.827
Goal identifies the bounded improvement to examine.

00:00:07.827 --> 00:00:12.523
Owners identifies authorization, monitoring, review, correction, stopping and escalation.

00:00:12.523 --> 00:00:15.654
Values states what must be protected.

00:00:15.654 --> 00:00:22.959
Evidence states the baseline, quality observations and participant actions that will inform a decision.

00:00:22.959 --> 00:00:28.177
Rules states permitted inputs, exclusions, required review and stop conditions.

00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:34.961
Notice explains the task, limits, support and question route under the actual policy.

00:00:34.961 --> 00:00:40.179
Compare these areas with the real roles and approved policy.

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:49.049
AI critique may suggest a missing measure or role; it cannot verify the policy or grant authority.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:52.180
Keep support and expertise dependencies visible.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:58.442
Retain one coherent adoption plan and test design in the continuing record.

00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:03.138
If approval remains unresolved, this is a simulated design.
